# Route for the media game. One shot per image format and per movie. Movie frames are identical, but the decoders and the
# time of the first frame differ between engines, so the movie shots are volatile (compared, reported, never failing).
# Ops: cmd TEXT | wait TOKEN | settle SECS | shot NAME [volatile] | note TEXT | quit
cmd auto on
cmd click on
wait menu True
cmd click off
settle 3
shot 01-menu
cmd start
after_start
cmd advance-to 2
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 02-png
cmd advance-to 3
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 03-jpg
cmd advance-to 4
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 04-webp
cmd advance-to 5
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 05-webp-lossless
cmd advance-to 6
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 06-avif
cmd advance-to 7
wait advance-done
settle 3
shot 07-movie-vp9 volatile
cmd advance-to 8
wait advance-done
settle 3
shot 08-movie-h264 volatile
cmd advance-to 9
wait advance-done
settle 3
shot 09-movie-theora volatile
cmd advance-to 10
wait advance-done
settle 3
shot 10-movie-av1 volatile
cmd advance-to 11
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 11-gif
cmd advance-to 12
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 12-gif-anim
cmd advance-to 13
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 13-alpha-png
cmd advance-to 14
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 14-alpha-webp
cmd advance-to 15
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 15-alpha-webp-lossless
cmd advance-to 16
wait advance-done
settle 2
shot 16-alpha-gif
quit
